  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    An intra-colonial war fought during the Orca Incursion era, triggered when the Icebound Exchange — Aurora Stack's dominant merchant guild — discovered the Radiant Ring, an artifact of considerable power, in the deep-ice and refused to submit it to the colony councils or the terms of the Flipper Accord. Holdborn (ice-thresh), the splinter faction advocating collective resource ownership, moved to claim the artifact first. The Exchange responded with Ice∴freeze, a Nightshelf-origin magic whose presence in merchant-guild hands has never been satisfactorily explained.
    
    ## Course
    
    The Forum Floe, Aurora Stack's principal deliberative ground, became the conflict's epicenter. Ice∴freeze magic fractured the floe's aurora-light into weaponized refraction; casualties shattered rather than burned. The Aurora Stack divided — Exchange loyalists against those defending Holdborn's collectivist claim — and E'frostlings, the former merchant-class faction, exploited the fracture to seize contested holdings. The Forum Floe was destroyed as a functional resource node.
    
    ## Aftermath
    
    The surface colony lost both the Floe and its capacity for self-sufficiency, leaving Aurora Stack dependent on Nightshelf fire-core supply — a dependency the Long-dark Edict's subsequent amendments attempted, without notable success, to regulate. The Swaleed~ Luminary, a ceremonial vessel held by the Cell, bears hairline frost-cracks identified as the earliest of three wars' damage scarred into its surface.
    
    Casualty figures from the Schism do not survive in any form I would call reliable. The ice-memory at the relevant Foundation stratum records intense thermal and acoustic disturbance, but the impressions are overlaid by Incursion-era deposits that make clean reading impossible. The numbers in circulation are inherited, not verified.
